emma: opened a tiny PR to tighten up SDK snippets across py/ts/go. includes consumer-side retry patterns, a null-cursor guard for Go pagination, and a short migration note for the v2 stream API. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/999
theo: can you paste the TS streaming example here so i can eyeball the await-for-await usage?
emma: sure:
```ts
// TS: async iterator streaming with consumer retry + jitter
import { Redwood } from '@redwood/inference'

async function show() {
  const client = new Redwood()
  let tries = 0
  while (tries < 3) {
    try {
      const stream = await client.stream('gpt-1', { prompt: 'hi' })
      for await (const chunk of stream) {
        process.stdout.write(chunk.text)
      }
      return
    } catch (err) {
      const backoff = (Math.random() + 0.5) * Math.pow(2, tries) * 100
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff))
      tries++
      if (tries === 3) throw err
    }
  }
}
```
